id: pm-csv-qnax
title: Adopt --respect-item-release in changelog scripts and close the shipped-but-stale export terminator tracker
description: "Adopts pm-changelog 2026.7.24 --respect-item-release across the changelog scripts and bumps the devDependency, then uses the new capability to close pm-csv-69ln, whose fix shipped in v2026.06.07 but whose tracker stayed open because closing it would have retro-dated the work into the current release window."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog,fleet-consistency,release-hygiene
created_at: "2026-07-24T21:34:17.382Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T21:34:18.200Z"
assignee: claude
author: claude
acceptance_criteria: "all four changelog scripts pass --respect-item-release; pm-changelog devDependency is ^2026.7.24; pm-csv-69ln is closed and appears under the 2026.6.7 heading not Unreleased; changelog:check green"
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:34:18.200Z",claude,"Verified with the PUBLISHED pm-changelog 2026.7.24 (what CI runs): regenerating places pm-csv-69ln under '## 2026.6.7 - 2026-06-07' as a Fixed entry, and changelog:check exits 0. The 69ln release field uses the padded git-tag spelling because 2026.7.24 compares release keys literally (pm-changelog pmc-2sfc / PR 94 fixes that; afterwards either spelling works). Underlying fix independently re-verified against real data before closing: excel export = 3 CRLF, 0 lone LF, ends CRLF; default export = 0 CR, LF only."
body: ""
